Yep — here’s a minimal HTML page that joins a LiveKit room using the token you generate.

1. `index.html`
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>LiveKit Call</title>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <style>
    body { font-family: system-ui; background: #0a0a0a; color: #fff; text-align: center; padding: 40px; }
    video { width: 45%; margin: 10px; border-radius: 12px; background: #000; }
    button { padding: 12px 20px; border: none; border-radius: 8px; background: #2563eb; color: white; font-size: 16px; cursor: pointer; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h2>LiveKit App-to-App Call</h2>
  <div id="videos"></div>
  <button id="joinBtn">Join Room</button>

  <script type="module">
    import { Room, RoomEvent, createLocalAudioTrack, createLocalVideoTrack } from 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/livekit-client@2.5.0/dist/livekit-client.esm.js';

    const LIVEKIT_URL = 'wss://YOUR-PROJECT.livekit.cloud'; // from LiveKit Cloud dashboard
    const TOKEN = 'PASTE_TOKEN_HERE'; // output from genToken.js

    const room = new Room();
    const videosDiv = document.getElementById('videos');

    room.on(RoomEvent.TrackSubscribed, (track, publication, participant) => {
      if (track.kind === 'video' || track.kind === 'audio') {
        const el = track.attach();
        videosDiv.appendChild(el);
      }
    });

    document.getElementById('joinBtn').onclick = async () => {
      await room.connect(LIVEKIT_URL, TOKEN);
      
      // Publish your camera + mic
      await room.localParticipant.enableCameraAndMicrophone();

      // Show your own video
      room.localParticipant.videoTrackPublications.forEach(pub => {
        const el = pub.track.attach();
        videosDiv.appendChild(el);
      });
    };
  </script>
</body>
</html>
2. How to use it
1. Replace `LIVEKIT_URL` with your LiveKit Cloud URL - looks like `wss://your-project.livekit.cloud`
2. Replace `TOKEN` with the JWT you got from running `node genToken.js`
3. Open the HTML file on 2 devices/browsers, both using tokens for the same `roomName`
4. Hit *Join Room* on both. You’ll see video/audio connect P2P through LiveKit

3. Important notes
- Keep this for testing only. In prod, you generate the token on your backend and fetch it via API. Never expose `API_SECRET` in the browser.
- If you want 0 mobile data usage, both devices must be on WiFi. Turn off mobile data to test.
- Free LiveKit Cloud tier gives you 10k participant-minutes/month. After that it charges $0.005/min.

